# Canonical identities. `git shortlog`, `git log` and most local tooling read
# this, so a commit that arrives from another clone still carrying the old
# address is displayed and counted under the right one.
#
# The address on the right of each line is the one that was written into
# history by mistake — a typo in a global git config, which put it on every
# commit from that machine for months. History has been rewritten, but Azeem's
# clone and any branch restored from a backup will still carry it.
#
# Note this file does NOT affect GitHub's contributor graph: that reads the raw
# author email out of each commit. Only rewriting history fixes attribution
# there, which is what was done.
Yar Muhammad Uwaim <yarmuhammaduwaim@gmail.com> <yarmuhammaduwaim@gmaill.com>
